  "question": {
    "text": "Match List-I with List-II :\n$\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline & \\text { List-I } & & \\text { List-II } \\\\\n\\hline \\text { (A) } & \\text { A force that restores an elastic body of unit area to its original state } & \\text { (I) } & \\text { Bulk modulus } \\\\\n\\hline \\text { (B) } & \\text { Two equal and opposite forces parallel to opposite faces } & \\text { (II) } & \\text { Young's modulus } \\\\\n\\hline \\text { (C) } & \\begin{array}{l}\n\\text { Forces perpendicular everywhere to the surface per unit area } \\\\\n\\text { same everywhere }\n\\end{array} & \\text { (III) } & \\text { Stress } \\\\\n\\hline \\text { (D) } & \\text { Two equal and opposite forces perpendicular to opposite faces } & \\text { (IV) } & \\text { Shear modulus } \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}$\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :",
